Bugfix: Store the mimetype part of malformed file cache mimetypes as unknown

A mimetype without a part before the slash, like `foo`, `0` or `/foo`, made the
file cache register an empty string as a new mimetype and use it as the
mimetype part of the file. Such files now get an unknown mimetype part (-1)
while their mimetype is kept. A mimetype that consists of blanks only or is not
a string at all is stored as unknown, like an empty one. When the mimetype of a
file becomes unknown, its mimetype part is reset as well, so a search for
images no longer finds a file whose type is not known anymore.
